  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "What Git Is and the Three Areas",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "What Git Is and the Three Areas",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Git Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Distributed== VCS: every clone holds the **full history**",
                "`commit`, `log`, `diff` work ==offline==",
                "A ==commit== = immutable snapshot of staged files",
                "It stores message, author, **parent pointer**, SHA-1 hash"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Three Areas",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Working tree",
                    "sub": "files on disk",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Staging (index)",
                    "sub": "next commit",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Repository",
                    "sub": ".git history",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Copies"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git add`",
                  "working tree → staging"
                ],
                [
                  "`git commit`",
                  "staging → repository"
                ],
                [
                  "`git restore <file>`",
                  "staging → working tree"
                ],
                [
                  "`git restore --staged <file>`",
                  "last commit (HEAD) → staging"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. File States",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Untracked",
                    "note": "new file",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Modified",
                    "note": "edited on disk",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Staged",
                    "note": "after add",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Committed",
                    "note": "after commit",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Which state?",
              "text": "`git status` tells you the state of every file. ==Run it before every commit.=="
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does Git work offline?** Every clone has the full history",
                "**Staging area?** The snapshot the next commit will contain"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core Workflow: init, clone, add, commit",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Core Workflow: init, clone, add, commit",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Start a Repo",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git init` creates a ==.git== folder in the current directory",
                "`git clone <url>` copies the **full repo** and sets remote ==origin=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Stage, Then Record",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Edit",
                    "sub": "working tree",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "git add",
                    "sub": "to staging",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "git commit",
                    "sub": "to repository",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Takes",
                "New files"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git add <file>`",
                  "one file",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "`git add .`",
                  "all under current dir",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "`git commit -m \"msg\"`",
                  "staged snapshot only",
                  "if staged"
                ],
                [
                  "`git commit -am \"msg\"`",
                  "tracked files only",
                  "{red:never}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==add== stages, ==commit== records the snapshot; `-am` skips untracked files"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git add notes.txt",
                "git commit -am \"Update docs\""
              ],
              "note": "new file needs add; -am covers tracked edits"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Good Commits and Amend",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One commit = ==one logical change==",
                "Imperative message: `Fix login redirect`",
                "`git commit --amend` rewrites the last commit's message or contents",
                "Amend only ==before pushing==: it creates a new hash"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Forgot a file?",
              "text": "`git add` it, then `git commit --amend --no-edit` to fold it into the last commit."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Inspecting State: status, log, diff",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Inspecting State: status, log, diff",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Status first",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git status` shows the ==branch==, {green:staged}, {orange:unstaged} and {red:untracked} files",
                "Run it ==before every commit==",
                "Not tracked yet: untracked. Edited but not added: unstaged"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. diff: which two areas",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Compares"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git diff`",
                  "working tree vs {blue:staging}"
                ],
                [
                  "`git diff --staged`",
                  "staging vs {green:last commit}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Reading history",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`--oneline --graph --all`: compact history, ==every branch==",
                "`log -p <file>`: the patches that changed ==one file==",
                "`show <hash>`: ==one commit==, message and patch"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git log --oneline --graph --all",
                "git log -p <file>",
                "git show <hash>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Undo with restore",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Copies",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git restore <file>`",
                  "staging → working tree",
                  "{red:discards} unstaged edits"
                ],
                [
                  "`git restore --staged <file>`",
                  "last commit → staging",
                  "unstages, ==keeps edits=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Irreversible",
              "text": "`git restore <file>` throws away unstaged edits for good. Run `git diff` first to see what you would lose."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Branches and Merging",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Branches and Merging",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Branch = Pointer",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==branch== is a movable pointer to a commit",
                "==HEAD== points to the branch you are on",
                "A new commit moves the current branch forward"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "C1",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "C2",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "C3",
                    "sub": "main",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HEAD",
                    "sub": "points to main",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Branch Commands",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git switch -c <name>`",
                  "create and switch"
                ],
                [
                  "`git branch`",
                  "list branches"
                ],
                [
                  "`git branch -d <name>`",
                  "delete a merged one"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Merge and Conflicts",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "`git merge <branch>`",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Linear history",
                  "==fast-forward=="
                ],
                [
                  "Diverged history",
                  "**merge commit**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Conflict leaves `<<<<<<<` `=======` `>>>>>>>` markers",
                "Edit the file, `git add` it, then `git commit`"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Before switching",
              "text": "Commit or ==stash== first: uncommitted changes may block the switch or follow you."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Is a branch a copy?** No, a pointer to a commit.",
                "**When does a merge fast-forward?** Linear history.",
                "**How do you resolve a conflict?** Edit, add, commit."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Remotes, Push/Pull and .gitignore",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Remotes, Push/Pull and .gitignore",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Remotes and Publishing",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==remote== is a named URL, usually `origin`",
                "`git remote -v` lists them",
                "`git push -u origin <branch>` publishes and sets the ==upstream==",
                "After that, plain `git push` works"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git remote -v",
                "git push -u origin feat/login",
                "git push"
              ],
              "note": "-u only the first time"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Fetch, Pull, Rejected Push",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "fetch",
                "pull"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Downloads commits",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Changes your files",
                  "{green:no}",
                  "{red:yes}, merges"
                ],
                [
                  "Equals",
                  "`git fetch`",
                  "fetch + merge (`--rebase`: rebase)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Push rejected: remote has commits you lack",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "git pull",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Resolve conflicts",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "git push",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Avoid `git push --force` on ==shared branches=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. .gitignore and Secrets",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Patterns skip untracked files: `node_modules/`, `*.log`, `.env`",
                "Already tracked files stay tracked: run `git rm --cached <file>` first"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Secrets",
              "text": "Never commit secrets. Once pushed, a later commit that deletes the file does ==not erase it from history==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
